---
// Kept as its own Astro component, rather than inline in the glossary MDX
// page, because MDX parses a `<style>` block's braces as JS expressions —
// scoped CSS only works cleanly from a plain `.astro` file.
---

<dl class="glossary-list">
  <div id="tacit-knowledge">
    <dt>Tacit knowledge</dt>
    <dd>
      What a practice requires that its documentation does not, and often
      cannot, state — because the person who wrote the documentation didn't
      need to state it to themselves. Polanyi's term; Collins' laser is the
      course's clearest demonstration of it.
    </dd>
  </div>

  <div id="capability">
    <dt>Capability</dt>
    <dd>
      The ability to actually do a thing, as distinct from the record of how
      it was once done. The course's central move is refusing to treat these
      as the same fact.
    </dd>
  </div>

  <div id="reinstatement">
    <dt>Reinstatement</dt>
    <dd>
      Deliberately rebuilding a capability an institution let lapse. Rarely
      free: reinstatement has a cost, and that cost is evidence the
      capability was really gone.
    </dd>
  </div>

  <div id="deskilling">
    <dt>Deskilling</dt>
    <dd>
      The reduction of a worker's skill and judgement as an organisational
      choice, usually made for efficiency or control — not, in Braverman's
      argument, an accident of technology.
    </dd>
  </div>

  <div id="automation-surprise">
    <dt>Automation surprise</dt>
    <dd>
      The moment an automated system hands control back to a person who has
      not had to exercise the underlying skill in years, at precisely the
      moment that skill is needed most. Bainbridge's irony, named.
    </dd>
  </div>

  <div id="institutional-memory">
    <dt>Institutional memory</dt>
    <dd>
      What an organisation still knows how to do, carried by the people and
      routines that do it — not by its filing system. The course's subject,
      and the thing the site's own name mocks by pretending an institution
      could simply teach a seminar about losing it.
    </dd>
  </div>
</dl>

<style>
  .glossary-list div {
    margin-block-end: 1.5rem;
  }

  .glossary-list dt {
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-block-end: 0.25rem;
  }

  .glossary-list dd {
    margin-inline-start: 0;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
  }
</style>
